// TWIN: keep in sync with ../localauthority/50-local.d/50-polaris-storage.pkla
// (that .pkla covers polkit < 0.106 / Ubuntu 22.04, which ignores this JS format).
//
// PolicyKit rule shipped by the polaris .deb. Grants the 'polaris' system user
// the ability to start the on-demand capture-disk unit, used by
// StorageSetupService when the browser POSTs /api/storage/prepare or
// /api/storage/format:
//
//   systemctl start polaris-storage-prep.service
//
// That unit (running as root) mounts a data disk and writes the fstab entry, or
// -- when the request says so explicitly -- partitions and formats a blank one,
// then exits.
//
// This file exists because STORAGE-1 assumed the self-update rule already
// covered it. It does not: 50-polaris-update.rules scopes its grant to
// action.lookup("unit") == "polaris-self-update.service", and on this appliance
// polkit is version 124, which reads .rules and IGNORES the broad manage-units
// grant in the .pkla twin. The result was "Interactive authentication required"
// on every attempt to set up a disk.
//
// Scope is intentionally narrow, matching the update / power / clock / network
// rules: only the polaris user, only this one unit. The unit itself re-derives
// every safety check from the kernel, so the grant does not widen what the
// unprivileged half can actually do.
polkit.addRule(function(action, subject) {
    if (subject.user != "polaris") return;

    if ((action.id == "org.freedesktop.systemd1.manage-units"
            || action.id == "org.freedesktop.systemd1.manage-unit-files")
        && action.lookup("unit") == "polaris-storage-prep.service") {
        return polkit.Result.YES;
    }
});
